Assuming you mean SLASH'EM, not SLASH, though in fact this
appears to apply to both:

There isn't (intentionally) any linkage between a Wizard's starting
spellbooks and his alignment, that I can see. The books are chosen on
a Chinese menu basis, a random pick from Column A, a random pick from
column B, and so on for four columns:

    A                B               C                    D
force bolt     resist poison    detect food          magic missile
sleep          resist sleep     detect monsters      confuse monster
                                light                slow monster
                                knock                cure blindness
                                wizard lock          endure heat
                                                     endure cold
                                                     insulate
                                                     create monster
                                                     healing

So, the chance of having no attack spell in your starting repertoire
should be 7/18. However, if you _are_ seeing a pattern in the
assignment of spellbooks, it may indicate that your system's RNG isn't
particularly R; pre-game set-up is when poor randomness can have the
most visible effects.

